From: Arsslen Idadi <arsslens021@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:47:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] focaltech_moh: support the old SIU bridge of 2808:93a9

2808:93a9 puts the FT9201 behind an older USB bridge than 2808:9338 and
2808:9348. It does not answer request 0x6F; its AFE registers are read with
0x3A instead (wIndex = register, the reply carries that register and the
next), and the frame is fetched with 0x35 (wValue = length, wIndex = 0x3400)
followed by a bulk read of width * height + 2 bytes, two header bytes first.
Its sensor is 96x96, AFE chip 0x95a8.

It also captures differently: a touch wakes the MCU, which scans once and
holds the frame until it sleeps again about 0.9 s later. While it holds one,
AFE 0x20 reads a5 5a and 0x1D reads 0xa0. The driver waits for that, reads
the frame, and first waits for any frame captured before the request to go,
so that only a touch made after it counts. 0x22 (0x70, 0x70), sent twice,
wakes the MCU, which open needs and which a sensor left in deep sleep by
another host needs too.

Open refuses a sensor whose 0x30 is not 0xbb, the value every unit seen so
far carries, rather than guess at setting one up, and any size but 96x96.
The bridge is told apart by product id, and everything that assumed 64x80
now takes the size from the device.
